{"id":10113,"name":"muk-alola","speciesId":89,"dex":89,"form":"alolan","generation":1,"types":["poison","dark"],"stats":{"hp":105,"attack":105,"defense":75,"special-attack":65,"special-defense":100,"speed":50},"abilities":[{"name":"poison-touch","hidden":false},{"name":"gluttony","hidden":false},{"name":"power-of-alchemy","hidden":true}],"height":10,"weight":520,"baseExp":175,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10113.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/10113.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/10113.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/10113.ogg","genus":"Sludge Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"Thickly covered with a filthy, vile sludge. It is so toxic, even its footprints contain poison."},{"version":"yellow","text":"Smells so awful, it can cause fainting. Through degeneration, it lost its sense of smell."},{"version":"gold","text":"They love to gath­ er in smelly areas where sludge ac­ cumulates, making the stench around them worse."},{"version":"silver","text":"Its body is made of a powerful poi­ son. Touching it accidentally will cause a fever that requires bed rest."},{"version":"crystal","text":"As it moves, a very strong poison leaks from it, making the ground there barren for three years."},{"version":"ruby","text":"From MUK’s body seeps a foul fluid that gives off a nose-bendingly horrible stench. Just one drop of this POKéMON’s body fluid can turn a pool stagnant and rancid."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"This POKéMON’s favorite food is anything that is repugnantly filthy. In dirty towns where people think nothing of throwing away litter on the streets, MUK are certain to gather."},{"version":"emerald","text":"It prefers warm and humid habitats. In the summertime, the toxic substances in its body intensify, making MUK reek like putrid kitchen garbage."},{"version":"firered","text":"It is usually undetectable because it blends in with the ground. Touching it can cause terrible poisoning."},{"version":"diamond","text":"A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid instantly kills plants and trees on contact."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"They love to gather in smelly areas where sludge accumulates, making the stench around them worse."},{"version":"soulsilver","text":"Its body is made of a powerful poison. Touching it accidentally will cause a fever that requires bed rest."},{"version":"black-2","text":"It’s so stinky! Muk’s body contains toxic elements, and any plant will wilt when it passes by."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"From Muk’s body seeps a foul fluid that gives off a nose-bendingly horrible stench. Just one drop of this Pokémon’s body fluid can turn a pool stagnant and rancid."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"This Pokémon’s favorite food is anything that is repugnantly filthy. In dirty towns where people think nothing of throwing away litter on the streets, Muk are certain to gather."},{"version":"sun","text":"The stench it gives off will make your nose scrunch up. Still, there are Muk fans who think that’s a good thing."},{"version":"moon","text":"After recent environmental improvements, this Pokémon is now hardly seen at all. People speculate that it may go extinct at some point."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"Their food sources have decreased, and their numbers have declined sharply. Sludge ponds are being built to prevent their extinction."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"Because they scatter germs everywhere, they’ve long been targeted for extermination, leading to a steep decline in their population."},{"version":"lets-go-pikachu","text":"Smells so awful, it can cause fainting. Through degeneration of its nose, it lost its sense of smell."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":75,"eggGroups":["indeterminate"],"isLegendary":false